{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And He brought her to the man.</b> From where did He bring her? Was she not taken from his ribs? Rather, the verse speaks according to the man's thought — for at first, when he saw her, he thought in his heart that she had been brought to him like the rest of the creatures, and when he perceived that he was missing his rib, then he said, עצם מעצמי etc. And similarly, והאנשים רדפו אחריהם — they thought to pursue after them. And one may say that she was built outside the Garden, and therefore it is written <b>and He brought her to the man</b> — from outside the Garden."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:33.640069251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}